{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-afb4f658-4eb5-475f-a6eb-97db2be01fe3","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-940b15f076efb0a6","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9020-e4pxg4sk/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9020-E001.md","content":"# AMD Instinct validation campaign: vLLM serving functional and performance parity\n\n## Description\n\nThis epic delivers the validation campaign on physical AMD Instinct hardware\nthat establishes functional and performance parity data for vLLM serving of the\nplatform's supported model set on ROCm, and produces the go/no-go scope for\nproductization. It is the strategy's decision gate: the productization of a\nsupported vLLM ROCm serving runtime proceeds for exactly the models this\ncampaign clears.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Secure access to dedicated AMD Instinct nodes (procurement or partner-lab\n  access) and stand up the ROCm system stack on them: ROCm drivers, the AMD GPU\n  operator / device plugin stack, and verification that `amd.com/gpu` resources\n  are discoverable and consumable by pods.\n- Select and record the vLLM ROCm runtime image used for the campaign (upstream\n  AMD-published or self-built) and its provenance, including the upstream ROCm\n  release it is based on.\n- For each model in the supported model set, exercise vLLM serving on ROCm and\n  record a pass/fail functional result (correct inference behavior on the\n  model's supported task surface).\n- For each functionally passing model, record performance measurements\n  (throughput and latency) and produce performance parity data relative to the\n  platform's CUDA runtime builds.\n- Produce the validation report: per-model functional and performance outcomes,\n  the ROCm stack and image versions used, and the resulting go/no-go\n  recommendation with the cleared model list for productization.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- The ROCm system stack (drivers and AMD GPU operator / device plugin) is\n  installed on the campaign's AMD Instinct nodes and verified to expose\n  `amd.com/gpu` resources that pods can request and use.\n- Every model in the supported model set has a recorded functional pass/fail\n  result for vLLM serving on ROCm.\n- Every functionally passing model has recorded performance measurements with\n  parity data relative to the CUDA runtime builds.\n- The validation report is delivered, stating per-model outcomes, the exact ROCm\n  stack and runtime image versions used, and a go/no-go recommendation with the\n  explicit cleared model list.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-1 (P0): fully covered — this epic is the validation campaign and produces\n  the go/no-go scope for productization.\n\n## Risks and Notes\n\n- Hardware access (procurement or partner-lab) is an externally controlled\n  availability precondition; securing it is part of this epic's work, but the\n  access being granted is not an acceptance condition on the deliverable.\n- Upstream ROCm image release cadence is controlled by AMD and the upstream\n  communities; the campaign records which images were used so the\n  productization decision can account for cadence.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":35867,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a07a6fa63d415b0f","agent_id":"ab43bec2ef90fc9be","session_id":"1580befd-2500-423d-8dd5-ee8176ac89f3","uuid":"1851641c-d0d3-4ef4-a734-66ea15d89427","timestamp":"2026-10-26T17:24:50.707Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9020 into epics"}
