{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-54aabc9f-80a7-418f-8921-d839f4549aa4","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-9aad757ee4a59a6c","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9020-e4pxg4sk/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9020-E002.md","content":"# Productize supported vLLM ROCm serving runtime\n\n## Description\n\nThis epic productizes a supported vLLM ROCm serving runtime for the models the\nAMD Instinct validation campaign clears: a released runtime image, its\nServingRuntime definition for KServe InferenceServices, and the image\nsourcing/rebase strategy relative to upstream ROCm release cadence.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Build and release a supported vLLM ROCm serving runtime image for the cleared\n  model set, through the existing Serving Runtimes build and release process.\n- Provide the ServingRuntime/ClusterServingRuntime definition that exposes the\n  ROCm runtime to KServe InferenceServices, requesting `amd.com/gpu` resources\n  on AMD GPU nodes.\n- Determine and document the runtime's image sourcing and rebase strategy\n  (upstream AMD-published ROCm images versus self-built), accounting for the\n  upstream ROCm release cadence relative to platform release trains.\n- Validate serving through KServe on AMD GPU nodes (KServe component\n  validation): the productized runtime deploys under InferenceServices and\n  serves predictions for the cleared model set.\n- Update any incidental runtime-related references (supported-accelerator\n  labels, image references) that fall out of this change.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- A supported vLLM ROCm serving runtime image is built and released for the\n  current platform version through the Serving Runtimes build pipeline, and the\n  pipeline run is green.\n- A ServingRuntime definition exposes the ROCm runtime, requesting\n  `amd.com/gpu` resources, and is accepted by the KServe CRD surface.\n- The productized runtime serves predictions through KServe InferenceServices\n  on AMD GPU nodes for every model on the cleared list from the validation\n  campaign.\n- The image sourcing and rebase strategy is documented and reproducible, stating\n  which upstream ROCm releases it tracks and the fallback when upstream cadence\n  does not align with a platform release train.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-2 (P0): fully covered — the supported vLLM ROCm serving runtime is\n  productized for the models the validation campaign clears.\n- Covers the KServe affected-component validation (passive component, same\n  team): serving on AMD nodes under KServe is verified here.\n\n## Risks and Notes\n\n- Scope is parameterized by the validation campaign's cleared model list; a\n  partial clear narrows the released model set, and a no-go descopes this epic.\n- Upstream ROCm image release timing is controlled by AMD and the upstream\n  communities and may not align with platform release trains; the documented\n  sourcing strategy must state the fallback.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":36665,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a07a6fa63d415b0f","agent_id":"ab43bec2ef90fc9be","session_id":"1580befd-2500-423d-8dd5-ee8176ac89f3","uuid":"b50f8463-2412-4478-9323-2b95704077fa","timestamp":"2026-10-26T17:25:00.305Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9020 into epics"}
