PyTorchJob requesting `amd.com/gpu` resources on a single GPU runs to\n54\t  successful completion on ROCm-enabled nodes.\n55\t- A multi-GPU (multi-worker) PyTorchJob requesting `amd.com/gpu` resources runs\n56\t  to successful completion on ROCm-enabled nodes.\n57\t- The above jobs are admitted through Kueue when queueing is enabled, and the\n58\t  admission behavior is recorded as a validation result.\n59\t- Any operator changes required for AMD GPU resource handling in PyTorchJob\n60\t  pods are implemented and covered by the validation above.\n61\t\n62\t## HLR Traceability\n63\t\n64\t- HLR-3 (P1, training portion): PyTorch training on ROCm is supported for\n65\t  single- and multi-GPU jobs admitted through Kueue.\n66\t\n67\t## Risks and Notes\n68\t\n69\t- Verification requires access to AMD GPU nodes; this epic can be implemented\n70\t  ahead of hardware availability but cannot be validated without it.\n71\t- The PyTorch ROCm worker images depend on upstream ROCm releases whose cadence\n72\t  is controlled by AMD and the upstream communities.\n73\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a6500e71cd098de2","agent_id":"a03f53f95020767ad","session_id":"1580befd-2500-423d-8dd5-ee8176ac89f3","uuid":"2fdbe70e-df85-4d00-a9a8-0457ad8ad995","timestamp":"2026-10-26T17:27:09.167Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-a0fce4503da7b2e9","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9020 decomposition"}
