{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-816ab2304a11c122","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9020-E004\n3\ttitle: Kueue amd.com/gpu quota handling for AMD GPU workloads\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9020\n5\tcomponent: Distributed Workloads\n6\tteam: Distributed Workloads\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tdependencies: []\n10\tai_signals:\n11\t  change_specificity: 1\n12\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n13\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n14\t  existing_foundation: 1\n15\t  open_questions: 0\n16\t  external_dependency: 0\n17\t  human_process_gates: 0\n18\t  repo_access: 1\n19\t  architecture_claims: 1\n20\timplementation_type: null\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 5\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# Kueue amd.com/gpu quota handling for AMD GPU workloads\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tThis epic delivers `amd.com/gpu` quota handling in the platform's Kueue-based\n34\tqueueing layer, so workloads requesting AMD GPU resources are admitted under\n35\tthe ClusterQueue/LocalQueue quota model like their NVIDIA counterparts.\n36\t\n37\t## Scope\n38\t\n39\t- Extend the Kueue quota configuration to cover `amd.com/gpu` resources:\n40\t  quota flavors and queue configuration for AMD GPU nodes within the existing\n41\t  ClusterQueue/LocalQueue model.\n42\t- Preserve existing admission semantics for AMD GPU workloads, including\n43\t  all-or-nothing (waitForPodsReady) admission and queueing when quota is\n44\t  exhausted.\n45\t- Verify on AMD GPU nodes that workloads requesting `amd.com/gpu` (for example\n46\t  PyTorchJobs) are admitted according to quota and run as admitted.\n47\t\n48\t## Acceptance Criteria\n49\t\n50\t- Kueue quota configuration supports `amd.com/gpu` resources within the\n51\t  ClusterQueue/LocalQueue quota model, and the configuration is delivered.\n52\t- A workload requesting `amd.com/gpu` is admitted when quota is available and\n53\t  queued (not partially admitted) when quota is exhausted.\n54\t- Admission of an AMD GPU workload preserves all-or-nothing readiness\n55\t  semantics.\n56\t- Verification on AMD GPU nodes is recorded: an `amd.com/gpu`-requesting\n57\t  workload is admitted under quota and runs to completion.\n58\t\n59\t## HLR Traceability\n60\t\n61\t- HLR-3 (P1, quota portion): `amd.com/gpu` quota handling for jobs admitted\n62\t  through Kueue.\n63\t\n64\t## Risks and Notes\n65\t\n66\t- Assumes `amd.com/gpu` resources are exposed on nodes by the AMD GPU\n67\t  operator / ROCm device plugin stack, which is not part of the platform\n68\t  inventory; the validation campaign covers standing it up on validation nodes.\n69\t- Verification requires access to AMD GPU nodes; the configuration work can be\n70\t  implemented ahead of hardware availability.\n71\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a6500e71cd098de2","agent_id":"a03f53f95020767ad","session_id":"1580befd-2500-423d-8dd5-ee8176ac89f3","uuid":"2be9f291-4e0e-4be0-81f8-afb311e08191","timestamp":"2026-10-26T17:27:10.183Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-816ab2304a11c122","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9020 decomposition"}
