rebase strategy\n51\t  (upstream AMD-published ROCm images versus self-built), accounting for the\n52\t  upstream ROCm release cadence relative to platform release trains.\n53\t- Validate serving through KServe on AMD GPU nodes (KServe component\n54\t  validation): the productized runtime deploys under InferenceServices and\n55\t  serves predictions for the cleared model set.\n56\t- Update any incidental runtime-related references (supported-accelerator\n57\t  labels, image references) that fall out of this change.\n58\t\n59\t## Acceptance Criteria\n60\t\n61\t- A supported vLLM ROCm serving runtime image is built and released for the\n62\t  current platform version through the Serving Runtimes build pipeline, and the\n63\t  pipeline run is green.\n64\t- A ServingRuntime definition exposes the ROCm runtime, requesting\n65\t  `amd.com/gpu` resources, and is accepted by the KServe CRD surface.\n66\t- The productized runtime serves predictions through KServe InferenceServices\n67\t  on AMD GPU nodes for every model on the cleared list from the validation\n68\t  campaign.\n69\t- The image sourcing and rebase strategy is documented and reproducible, stating\n70\t  which upstream ROCm releases it tracks and the fallback when upstream cadence\n71\t  does not align with a platform release train.\n72\t\n73\t## HLR Traceability\n74\t\n75\t- HLR-2 (P0): fully covered — the supported vLLM ROCm serving runtime is\n76\t  productized for the models the validation campaign clears.\n77\t- Covers the KServe affected-component validation (passive component, same\n78\t  team): serving on AMD nodes under KServe is verified here.\n79\t\n80\t## Risks and Notes\n81\t\n82\t- Scope is parameterized by the validation campaign's cleared model list; a\n83\t  partial clear narrows the released model set, and a no-go descopes this epic.\n84\t- Upstream ROCm image release timing is controlled by AMD and the upstream\n85\t  communities and may not align with platform release trains; the documented\n